# C++ Matrix Traversals Cheatsheet

`int n = matrix.size();` (rows), `int m = matrix[0].size();` (cols)

Examples use:
```
1 2 3
4 5 6
7 8 9
```

## Row-major (standard)
```cpp
// left-to-right, top-to-bottom. The default scan.
// use: visit every cell, summing, searching, copying
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    for (int j = 0; j < m; j++)
        // matrix[i][j]
// Time O(n*m), Space O(1)
```
```
order: 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9

→ → →
→ → →
→ → →
```

## Column-major
```cpp
// top-to-bottom, then next column. Outer loop is columns.
// use: column-wise aggregation, processing data stored by column
for (int j = 0; j < m; j++)
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
        // matrix[i][j]
// Time O(n*m), Space O(1)
```
```
order: 1 4 7 2 5 8 3 6 9

↓ ↓ ↓
↓ ↓ ↓
↓ ↓ ↓
```

## Transpose (swap across main diagonal)
```cpp
// flip rows<->cols. Square matrix only for in-place.
// use: step 1 of rotate-90, mirroring across diagonal
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    for (int j = i; j < n; j++)        // j = i avoids undoing swaps
        swap(matrix[i][j], matrix[j][i]);
// Time O(n^2/2) = O(n^2), Space O(1)
```
```
1 2 3        1 4 7
4 5 6   ->   2 5 8
7 8 9        3 6 9
```

## Rotate 90 clockwise (transpose + reverse rows)
```cpp
// transpose, then reverse each row
// use: image rotation in-place
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    for (int j = i; j < n; j++)
        swap(matrix[i][j], matrix[j][i]);
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    reverse(matrix[i].begin(), matrix[i].end());
// Time O(n^2), Space O(1)
```
```
1 2 3        7 4 1
4 5 6   ->   8 5 2
7 8 9        9 6 3
```

## Rotate 90 counter-clockwise (transpose + reverse cols)
```cpp
// transpose, then reverse each column (reverse order of rows)
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    for (int j = i; j < n; j++)
        swap(matrix[i][j], matrix[j][i]);
reverse(matrix.begin(), matrix.end());   // reverses the rows
// Time O(n^2), Space O(1)
```
```
1 2 3        3 6 9
4 5 6   ->   2 5 8
7 8 9        1 4 7
```

## Main diagonal
```cpp
// top-left to bottom-right. Cells where i == j.
// use: diagonal sums, identity checks (square matrix)
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    // matrix[i][i]
// Time O(n), Space O(1)
```
```
